# ask_user_question: the model asks a single multiple-choice question,
# kiln shows the inline question prompt (permission_render.go's visual
# language reused for it - askuser_render.go), the first option is picked
# with a digit key, and the model's reply after the answer lands. A single
# question ends the exchange directly (no review screen - that only shows
# up with more than one question, exercised separately below).
@faux testdata/faux/qa/tools-askuser-question.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE decide how to fix the bug
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Which approach should I use\?/ 20
SHOT question-first-option-selected
EXPECT /Fast path/
EXPECT /Careful path/
EXPECT /Other/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
KEY down
SHOT question-second-option-selected
KEY 1
WAITFOR /Got it, going with the fast path\./ 20
SHOT after-answer
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
